---
Conway's Life, wrapping at the edges, in text. **1.8KB** of wasm.

**space** runs it, **n** steps once, **r** reseeds. The seeding is `xorshift32`,
so a given seed always grows the same garden.

## why this is here

A garden should contain something that is alive and not being steered. The
rules are four lines; everything you will watch it do is emergent from them,
and none of it is authored.

The population counter is exported so the page can notice when the board dies
or freezes — which it usually does, eventually. That is also the point.

See [[mandelbrot|the set]] and [[crossword]].
